{"id": "EUVD-2026-82186", "enisaUuid": "e0561de2-3d99-3399-be0a-7228e8682bdb", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndax/fsdev: clear vmemmap_shift when binding static pgmap\n\nClear pgmap->vmemmap_shift for static DAX devices. When rebinding a static\ndevice from device_dax (which may set vmemmap_shift based on alignment) to\nfsdev_dax, the stale vmemmap_shift persists on the shared pgmap. Explicitly\nzero it before devm_memremap_pages() so the vmemmap is built for order-0\nfolios as fsdev requires.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:05:11", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d298a0513aaf7d48f2a9f4a90041de910750cfcf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e0239229931faf9ca3367e3befcf16f77b2cd45b"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93076", "GHSA-m5cm-762c-jpjj"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "14843637-c777-3d1e-9044-4ebcb8cd2b23", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.1"}, {"id": "33d24b22-e3dd-3ac4-a2bf-09556363f281", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3cac096d-369e-36da-a059-f782d8d6887b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d5406bd458b0ac10b1301a4d5801d85c8f648637 <e0239229931faf9ca3367e3befcf16f77b2cd45b"}, {"id": "46bcafe8-040c-35e3-88c8-e2359f4b06ad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d5406bd458b0ac10b1301a4d5801d85c8f648637 <d298a0513aaf7d48f2a9f4a90041de910750cfcf"}, {"id": "a7e5857d-a9bf-3919-8b7c-0ec88cbf5541", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d17fe431-8cc4-33a3-aceb-b3d0c292d3ea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "17e405f2-d0f6-3665-b841-f37ddc2d334f", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}]